✅ Program 19-Real-Time Application 3: Input Validation Service

📌 Description

A business application often needs to validate different types of user data such as marks, payment amounts, and names.

This program uses a common "validate()" function name with different parameter types.

The compiler selects the appropriate overloaded function depending on the argument passed.

🎯 OOP Concepts Used

- 🔹 Function overloading
- 🔹 Compile-time polymorphism
- 🔹 String processing
- 🔹 Input validation
- 🔹 Encapsulation

💡 Key Point

Different types of data can be validated using the same "validate()" interface through function overloading.
